============================================================================
        CNet Lexicon Interpretor, v1.5 HISTORY! File by Dotoran!
============================================================================

-- v1.5 --
    - File now reads the Editor Temp Path directly from CNet, so having to
      specify the path is no longer needed.
    - The launch command now takes an argument(0 or 1), which determines if
      LEX should run automatically or ask the user first. This does away with
      another of the variables from v1.0, as it is now possibly to have LEX
      auto for some places, but polite in others.
    - Uses of the MCI {$ } command were replaced with ADDRESS COMMAND, so as
      to make it compatible on newer Amiga Systems, which seem to frown on
      the {$ } command.
    - New features this version include:
        - A "LEX" command, which takes a path/filename as an argument. The
          SysOp can now LEX-Check any text file they wish.
        - Your remote users can use an argument of UPLOAD to initiate an
          XMODEM upload of any text files they wish to have LEX-Checked!
        - All users can also specify a ? as the argument for a brief account
          of possible formats for use with this command.
        - Coding was cleaned up and tightened up, so as to be shorter and
          faster than previous versions.
    - Release Date: December 11, 1994

-- v1.1 --
    - Never officially released.
    - This was the version that made the Editor Path internal, without the
      need for a SysOp defined variable.

-- v1.0 --
    - Release Date: September 1, 1993
    - Allowed CNet Amiga to use the "LEX" dos file to interpret the read-
      ability levels of user written messages.
    - Included means to change colors, whether or not the user was asked if
      they wished to use LEX or not, Access Groups to SKIP using LEX as well
      as well as specifying the temp directory to use.

